# Starting a Copied PostgreSQL 16 Data Directory: Startup Errors & Fixes

A hands-on log of what happened when I copied a PostgreSQL 16 data directory over to another Ubuntu machine and tried to start the server with `pg_ctl`.

Copying a data directory (`PGDATA`) moves database files and configuration references—not OS packages, system locales, shared PostgreSQL files, SSL certificates, or temporary `/var/run` directories. Running `pg_ctl` directly surfaces these checks one by one.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Error

LOG:  could not open configuration directory "/etc/postgresql/16/main/conf.d": No such file or directory
FATAL:  configuration file "/etc/postgresql/16/main/postgresql.conf" contains errors

And inspecting line 812 of postgresql.conf showed an empty value after =

include_dir =

reason: 

postgresql.conf included an include_dir setting without a valid directory path (or pointing to conf.d which didn't exist). PostgreSQL treats a missing include_dir target or malformed directive as a startup error.

Fix: 

Either set a valid directory and create it (or comment out include_dir if unused): {i commented the line --> #include_dir = 'conf.d'}
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Error:

LOG:  invalid value for parameter "lc_messages": "en_US.UTF-8"
LOG:  invalid value for parameter "lc_monetary": "en_US.UTF-8"
LOG:  invalid value for parameter "lc_numeric": "en_US.UTF-8"
LOG:  invalid value for parameter "lc_time": "en_US.UTF-8"
FATAL:  configuration file "/etc/postgresql/16/main/postgresql.conf" contains errors

locale -a only listed C, C.utf8, and POSIX, and /etc/locale.gen didn't exist until the locales package was installed.

Fix:

sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y locales
sudo sed -i 's/^# *en_US.UTF-8 UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8 UTF-8/' /etc/locale.gen
sudo locale-gen

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Error:

FATAL:  could not open directory "/usr/share/postgresql/16/timezonesets": No such file or directory
HINT:  This may indicate an incomplete PostgreSQL installation, or that the file "/usr/lib/postgresql/16/bin/postgres" has been moved away from its proper location.

Fix:

copied the directory from the primary using scp -r 

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Error:

FATAL:  could not load server certificate file "/etc/ssl/certs/ssl-cert-snakeoil.pem": No such file or directory
LOG:  database system is shut down

Fix:

sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y ssl-cert
ls -l /etc/ssl/certs/ssl-cert-snakeoil.pem

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Error:

FATAL:  could not access private key file "/etc/ssl/private/ssl-cert-snakeoil.key": Permission denied
LOG:  database system is shut down

Fix:

sudo usermod -aG ssl-cert postgres

